posts.body:
Have to agree with the consensus that people only hate on the RTP because it's been used for so many low effort shovelware games. And also that it gets much better with some edits or additions like Avery said. Here's an unfinished map I made - unfinished because while I wanted a hilly forested area, it came out looking a bit too cliff-like for my plans. But even so, considering mapping is one of my weaker spots skill-wise and I need to keep practicing at it, I think it was coming along really rather well. On this map the only paid DLC I used was
the Essentials Set.
Everything else is a mix of the MV and MZ RTP and free assets from the community, namely from
@Avery
@Candacis
and PandaMaru (give credit where credit is due). I was pretty happy with how it was looking other than it just wasn't feeling foresty enough (skill issue on my part). So yeah, nothing wrong with the RTP at all, just need to take the time to tweak it a little and add in a few more matching resources, of which there are plenty available here.
